    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0769" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Colonel Marshall S. Carter </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-13">13 September 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1489. According to information available here, one of the three programs
                    authorized under the Lend Lease 3 (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) clause is the
                    continuation of the training and equipment program. Training equipment for 10
                    Communist Divisions is a part of that program and the equipment, about 300 tons,
                    is already in Peiping. However, turnover under the 3 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >c</hi>) clause is supposed to be effected by 31st October 1946. The
                    Generalissimo, see CFBX 28398 dated 13 April,<anchor n="63" xml:id="d435-f1"/>
                    refused to accept the Communist equipment under Lend Lease until reorganization
                    and integration of these forces began, which cannot take place before 31
                    October. Other indications would also suggest delays past 31st October.</p>
                <p>Please notify appropriate War Department agencies of this situation and request
                    they endeavor to devise some legal means of turnover of this equipment sometime
                    after 31st October 1946.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
